module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohOverAlgebra.RestrictScalars
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.QuasicoherentPushforwardExactSequence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.QuasicoherentSheavesProperties

/-!
# Free modules and kernels over a sheaf of algebras are quasi-coherent on the base

Let `F` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site `B`, let
`α : 𝒪_F ⟶ A` be an arbitrary morphism from the structure sheaf of the small étale site of `F`
to a sheaf of rings `A` on that site, and suppose `A` itself is quasi-coherent as an
`𝒪_F`-module.  This file proves two closure facts about the `𝒪_F`-module obtained from an
`A`-module by restriction of scalars along `α`:

* a free `A`-module restricts to a quasi-coherent `𝒪_F`-module, and
* the kernel of a morphism of `A`-modules whose two restrictions of scalars are quasi-coherent
  restricts to a quasi-coherent `𝒪_F`-module.

Both are steps in the proof of the second assertion of Stacks Tag 08AI — that an `A`-module is
quasi-coherent as an `𝒪_F`-module exactly when it is quasi-coherent as an `A`-module — and they
are the two facts that its hard direction needs in order to see that the *relations* between the
generators of an `A`-module are again generated by sections over an affine chart.  The
Zariski form of the same argument is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohLimits.isQuasicoherent_restrictScalars_iff`.

Both proofs are formal.  Restriction of scalars preserves colimits
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RestrictScalarsColimits.preservesColimitsOfShape_restrictScalars`),
so it carries the colimiting cofan exhibiting a free `A`-module as a direct sum of copies of the
unit `A`-module to a colimiting cofan on the constant family at the restriction of scalars of
that unit, and a direct sum of quasi-coherent `𝒪_F`-modules is quasi-coherent by clause (1) of
Stacks 03M1, which is unconditional for this site as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isColimit_cofan`.  Restriction of scalars also
preserves finite limits
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohOverAlgebra.preservesFiniteLimits_restrictScalars`), so the
kernel comparison is an isomorphism, and the kernel of a morphism of quasi-coherent `𝒪_F`-modules
is quasi-coherent by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_kernel_of_quasicoherent`,
which rests on Descent, Proposition 03DX (2) for this site.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_restrictScalars_free`: **a free `A`-module is
  quasi-coherent as an `𝒪_F`-module** as soon as `A` is.  The index type lies in the universe of
  the schemes, which is where Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.free` lives.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_restrictScalars_kernel`: **the kernel of a
  morphism of `A`-modules is quasi-coherent as an `𝒪_F`-module** when the two restrictions of
  scalars are.

## Implementation notes

The quasi-coherence of `A` as an `𝒪_F`-module is a hypothesis rather than an instance, and `A`
is an arbitrary sheaf of rings with an arbitrary morphism from the structure sheaf, exactly as in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/QuasicoherentOverAlgebraChartGenerators.lean`.  At
`A = f_*𝒪_Y` for an affine morphism `f : Y ⟶ X` of algebraic spaces the hypothesis is discharged
by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_restrictScalars_structureRingSheafDirectImage`.

The colimiting cofan of a free module is passed through
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Cofan.isColimitMapCoconeEquiv` rather than used as a
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Cocone` over a discrete diagram, because
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isColimit_cofan` consumes a
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Cofan` on the family and the image of `SheafOfModules.freeCofan` under a
functor is a cocone on the mapped diagram; the two differ by that equivalence only.

The kernel is compared with the kernel of the restricted morphism through
`CategoryTheory.Limits.kernelComparison`, as an isomorphism rather than an equality: restriction
of scalars does not change the underlying sheaf of abelian groups, but the kernel is specified by
its universal property in each of the two categories of modules, so the comparison is what the
statement needs.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08AI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08AI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0H88](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0H88)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03M1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03M1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)
    {F : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {hF : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS F}
    {A : Sheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).J RingCat.{u}}
    (α : Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS F hF).O ⟶ A)

/-- **A free `A`-module is quasi-coherent as an `𝒪_F`-module** as soon as `A` is: restriction of
scalars preserves colimits, so it carries the colimiting cofan exhibiting the free `A`-module on
a type `I` as a direct sum of `I` copies of the unit `A`-module to a colimiting cofan on the
constant family at the restriction of scalars of that unit, and a direct sum of quasi-coherent
`𝒪_F`-modules is quasi-coherent. -/
theorem isQuasicoherentOnSite_restrictScalars_free
    (hA : ((SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u} α).obj
      (SheafOfModules.unit A)).IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (I : Type u) :
    ((SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u} α).obj
      (SheafOfModules.free.{u} (R := A) I)).IsQuasicoherentOnSite := by
  have hc : IsColimit (Cofan.mk
      ((SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u} α).obj (SheafOfModules.free.{u} (R := A) I))
      (fun i : I ↦ (SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u} α).map (SheafOfModules.ιFree i))) :=
    (Cofan.isColimitMapCoconeEquiv (SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u} α) _
      (Cofan.mk (SheafOfModules.free.{u} (R := A) I) SheafOfModules.ιFree)).toFun
      (isColimitOfPreserves _ (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan I))
  exact isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isColimit_cofan B S hS F hF _ hc fun _ ↦ hA

/-- **The kernel of a morphism of `A`-modules is quasi-coherent as an `𝒪_F`-module** when the
two restrictions of scalars are: restriction of scalars preserves finite limits, so the kernel
comparison is an isomorphism, and the kernel of a morphism of quasi-coherent `𝒪_F`-modules is
quasi-coherent. -/
theorem isQuasicoherentOnSite_restrictScalars_kernel {M N : SheafOfModules.{u} A} (φ : M ⟶ N)
    (hM : ((SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u} α).obj M).IsQuasicoherentOnSite)
    (hN : ((SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u} α).obj N).IsQuasicoherentOnSite) :
    ((SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u} α).obj (kernel φ)).IsQuasicoherentOnSite :=
  have := hM
  have := hN
  SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherentOnSite.of_iso
    (asIso (kernelComparison φ (SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u} α))).symm
    (isQuasicoherentOnSite_kernel_of_quasicoherent B S hS F hF
      ((SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u} α).map φ))

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
